==English==
{{wikipedia|dialectic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|διαλεκτική||the art of argument through interactive questioning and answering|tr=dialektike|lang=grc}}, from {{term|διαλεκτικός|tr=dialektikos||competent debater|lang=grc}}, from {{term|διαλέγομαι|tr=dialegomai||to participate in a [[dialogue]]|lang=grc}}, from {{term|διά|tr=dia||inter, through|lang=grc}} + {{term|λέγειν|tr=legein||to speak|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{plural of|dialectic|lang=en}}[[Category:English plurals]]
# A [[systematic]] method of [[argument]] that attempts to [[resolve]] the [[contradiction]]s in [[opposing]] [[view]]s or [[idea]]s.

====Synonyms====
* [[dialectic]]
* [[dialectical method]]

